<title>USA: Illinois corn, soy harvests near completion.</title>
<headline>Illinois corn, soy harvests near completion.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snow slowed harvesting in northern Illinois during the week ended Sunday, but corn and soybean harvest advanced elsewhere and was nearly finished statewide, according to the state's Agricultural Statistics Service.</p>
<p>Corn was 92 percent harvested versus 99 a year ago and the 92 average.</p>
<p>Soybeans were 98 percent harvested versus 100 a year ago and the 99 average.</p>
<p>Sorghum was 80 percent harvested versus 95 a year ago and the 94 average.</p>
<p>Wheat seeding reached 99 percent and emergence 94 percent, versus 100 and 96 a year ago, and the 98 and 92 five-year averages. The wheat was rated 17 percent excellent, 61 good, 19 fair, one poor and two very poor.</p>
<p>Topsoil moisture was rated 12 percent surplus, 75 adequate, 12 short and one very short.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720--</p>
